From e865219d8ba875fcee3d017ff73e9ba28218cb42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:15:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve manager-less profiling before steering graph
 dispatch

Replay baseline: r6x author head 7316c7f9fae1bc4a0b7ab1848de0db4143eec5d2 and preceding
0500-series downstream patches. The original base and validation entries
below are historical provenance; r6x qualification is recorded separately.

Base: downstream steering candidate b9d59d9d2 on the complete 182-patch
r6v and request-steering series.
Rationale: initial profile_run calls _dummy_run and execute_model before
initialize_kv_cache constructs the graph manager. Preserve the existing
manager-less eager descriptor without selecting or calling a graph manager;
leave initialized graph routing unchanged.
Quality: no request, precision, profile, kernel or capacity changes. Execute
the complete production profile_run, _dummy_run, execute_model, descriptor
and dispatch bodies in a CPU fixture with device boundaries substituted.
Cover loaded/unloaded profiles and explicit/default KV budgets, real model
input preparation and the rejection of manager-less non-profile dispatch.
Validation: all four regression cases fail on the prior candidate's assert
and pass after this fix; the local CPU source collection has 108 passing
checks. GPU startup, CED/SP integration and throughput remain unqualified.
Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
